  "derivation": [
   "Transfer VADC=(100/133)*(VDD/2+CV/8) and inverse CV=10.64*VADC-4*VDD: engineering/a5/electronics/reports/electrical_margins.json cv_transfer (kept unchanged).",
   "One 12-bit code at 3.3 V is 0.806 mV at the ADC pin, 8.57 mV of CV.",
   "Firmware CV deadband is +/-50 mV and full scale +/-5 V (engineering/a5/firmware/README.md mode table, LB_CV_DEADBAND_MV in src/light_block.c). Half a code (4.3 mV CV) is under 9 % of the deadband, so an LED-brightness-dependent reference shift of that size cannot move a 0 V input out of the deadband or feed back visibly; one code total (8.6 mV CV) is 17 %.",
   "A static offset is removable by the firmware zero calibration (lb_calibration_t); the LED-dependent part is not, hence the tighter half-code allocation for it.",
   "The same allocations were already the screen of this script; this revision requires them at the hot/thin-copper corner instead of nominal 20 C (the earlier Route2 candidate failed that)."
  ],
  "excluded": "Power-cable and connector contact resistance, op-amp offset, ADC/reference error, resistor tolerance, AC noise. Those are the same for any layout and belong to bench work (#10)."
